Cascade — a web UI for rtorrent, with rtorrent itself in the image.

Usage:
  docker run \
    -d \
    --name=cascade \
    -e PUID=1000 \
    -e PGID=1000 \
    -e TZ=Europe/Stockholm \
    -e WEB_USER=admin \
    -e WEB_PASS=change-me \
    -e RT_PORT_RANGE=50000-50000 \
    -p 8080:8080 \
    -p 50000:50000 \
    -p 50000:50000/udp \
    -v /home/torrent/config:/config \
    -v /home/torrent/downloads:/downloads \
    -v /home/torrent/watch:/watch \
    --restart unless-stopped \
    --stop-timeout 60 \
    ghcr.io/johanlindvall/cascade:latest

Volumes:
  /config     rtorrent session, log, and Cascade state — keep this one
  /downloads  where the data lands
  /watch      .torrent files dropped here are loaded and started

Ports:
  8080        the web UI and API (WEB_PORT)
  50000       peer traffic, TCP and UDP (RT_PORT_RANGE)

Everything else is an environment variable (-e NAME=value). Only what you
set is applied; anything left unset keeps the default shown below.

PATHS AND IDENTITY
  PUID                       User id rtorrent and the web server run as [1000]
  PGID                       Group id rtorrent and the web server run as [1000]
  TZ                         Container timezone [UTC]
  RT_DOWNLOAD_DIR            Default download directory [/downloads]
  RT_COMPLETED_DIR           Move finished downloads here [unset]
  RT_SESSION_DIR             rtorrent's session state [/config/session]
  RT_WATCH_DIR               .torrent files dropped here are loaded and started [/watch]
  RT_WATCH_ENABLE            Set 0 to ignore the watch directory [1]
  RT_WATCH_INTERVAL          Watch-directory poll interval: seconds, MM:SS or HH:MM:SS [10]
  RT_LOG_FILE                rtorrent's log file, surfaced in the UI [/config/rtorrent.log]
  RT_LOG_LEVEL               Log scopes: info, debug, dht_debug, tracker_debug, … (more can be
                             raised live from the log dialog) [info]
  RT_UMASK                   umask rtorrent creates files with, in octal [0022]
  CASCADE_STATE_FILE         Preferences, progress, add times and throttle groups
                             [/config/cascade-state.json]
  CASCADE_CHOWN_DOWNLOADS    Set 1 to chown the download directory at startup (slow on large
                             libraries) [0]
  RT_SESSION_LOCK_KEEP       Set 1 to keep a leftover rtorrent.lock instead of clearing it [0]

BANDWIDTH AND SLOTS
  Rates are in KiB/s; 0 means unlimited.
  RT_DOWNLOAD_RATE           Global download limit [rtorrent default]
  RT_UPLOAD_RATE             Global upload limit [rtorrent default]
  RT_MAX_UPLOADS             Upload slots per torrent [rtorrent default]
  RT_MIN_UPLOADS             Minimum upload slots per torrent [rtorrent default]
  RT_MAX_UPLOADS_GLOBAL      Upload slots across all torrents [rtorrent default]
  RT_MAX_DOWNLOADS           Download slots per torrent [rtorrent default]
  RT_MIN_DOWNLOADS           Minimum download slots per torrent [rtorrent default]
  RT_MAX_DOWNLOADS_GLOBAL    Download slots across all torrents [rtorrent default]

PEERS
  RT_MIN_PEERS               Minimum peers while leeching [rtorrent default]
  RT_MAX_PEERS               Maximum peers while leeching [rtorrent default]
  RT_MIN_PEERS_SEED          Minimum peers while seeding (-1 disables) [rtorrent default]
  RT_MAX_PEERS_SEED          Maximum peers while seeding (-1 disables) [rtorrent default]
  RT_PEX                     Peer exchange, yes/no [rtorrent default]

NETWORK
  RT_PORT_RANGE              Incoming peer port range [50000-50000]
  RT_PORT_RANDOM             Pick a random port from the range, yes/no [no]
  RT_PORT_OPEN               Open the listening port, yes/no (removed in rtorrent 0.16)
                             [rtorrent default]
  RT_ENCRYPTION              e.g. allow_incoming,try_outgoing,enable_retry [rtorrent default]
  RT_BIND                    Bind address for outgoing connections [unset]
  RT_IP                      Address reported to trackers [unset]
  RT_BIND_IPV4               IPv4 bind address (rtorrent 0.16+) [unset]
  RT_BIND_IPV6               IPv6 bind address (rtorrent 0.16+) [unset]
  RT_PROXY                   HTTP proxy for tracker announces [unset]
  RT_PROXY_HTTP              Proxy for all HTTP traffic (rtorrent 0.16+) [unset]
  RT_PROXY_GLOBAL            Proxy for all traffic (rtorrent 0.16+) [unset]
  RT_BLOCK_OUTGOING          yes refuses outgoing connections (rtorrent 0.16+) [rtorrent
                             default]

TRACKERS AND DHT
  RT_DHT                     disable, off, auto or on [rtorrent default]
  RT_DHT_PORT                DHT UDP port [rtorrent default]
  RT_DHT_OVERRIDE_PORT       Announce a different DHT port (rtorrent 0.16+) [rtorrent default]
  RT_UDP_TRACKERS            Allow UDP trackers, yes/no [rtorrent default]
  RT_TRACKER_NUMWANT         Peers requested per announce (-1 leaves it to the tracker)
                             [rtorrent default]
  RT_HTTP_CAPATH             Directory of CA certificates for tracker TLS [unset]
  RT_HTTP_CACERT             CA bundle file for tracker TLS [unset]
  RT_SSL_VERIFY_PEER         Verify tracker TLS certificates, yes/no [rtorrent default]
  RT_SSL_VERIFY_HOST         Verify tracker TLS hostnames, yes/no [rtorrent default]

STORAGE
  RT_PREALLOCATE             Preallocate files, yes/no [rtorrent default]
  RT_HASH_ON_COMPLETION      Re-verify on completion, yes/no [rtorrent default]
  RT_ADVISE_RANDOM_HASHING   Random-access hint while hashing, yes/no (rtorrent 0.16+) [rtorrent
                             default]
  RT_MEMORY_MAX              Piece memory cap, bytes [rtorrent default]
  RT_MAX_FILE_SIZE           Largest accepted file, bytes [rtorrent default]
  RT_SYNC_TIMEOUT            Piece disk-sync timeout, seconds [rtorrent default]
  RT_PRELOAD_TYPE            Piece preload: 0 off, 1 madvise, 2 direct paging [rtorrent default]
  RT_PRELOAD_MIN_SIZE        Only preload torrents above this piece size, bytes [rtorrent
                             default]
  RT_PRELOAD_MIN_RATE        Only preload above this upload rate, bytes/s [rtorrent default]

RESOURCE LIMITS
  RT_MAX_OPEN_FILES          Open file handle cap [rtorrent default]
  RT_MAX_OPEN_SOCKETS        Open socket cap [rtorrent default]
  RT_MAX_HTTP_OPEN           Concurrent HTTP requests (read-only on rtorrent 0.16+) [rtorrent
                             default]
  RT_HTTP_MAX_HOST           HTTP connections per host (rtorrent 0.16+) [rtorrent default]
  RT_DNS_CACHE_TIMEOUT       DNS cache lifetime, seconds [rtorrent default]
  RT_RECEIVE_BUFFER          Socket receive buffer, bytes [rtorrent default]
  RT_SEND_BUFFER             Socket send buffer, bytes [rtorrent default]

RPC
  RT_SCGI_SOCKET             Unix socket rtorrent listens on, unless RT_SCGI_PORT is set
                             [/run/rtorrent/rpc.socket]
  RT_SCGI_PORT               Listen for SCGI on this TCP port instead of the socket
                             (unauthenticated — keep it private) [unset]
  RT_SCGI_BIND               Address RT_SCGI_PORT listens on; 0.0.0.0 lets a published port
                             reach it [127.0.0.1]
  RT_XMLRPC_SIZE_LIMIT       Max XML-RPC request size, bytes (raises the .torrent upload
                             ceiling) [16777216]
  CASCADE_SCGI               Endpoint the web server talks to — a path, or host:port for a
                             remote rtorrent [RT_SCGI_SOCKET, or RT_SCGI_PORT (on 127.0.0.1 for
                             a wildcard RT_SCGI_BIND)]

WEB SERVER
  WEB_PORT                   HTTP port [8080]
  WEB_HOST                   Bind address [0.0.0.0]
  WEB_USER                   Basic-auth user; auth is enabled only when both are set [unset (no
                             auth)]
  WEB_PASS                   Basic-auth password [unset (no auth)]
  WEB_BASE_PATH              Serve under a sub-path, e.g. /rtorrent [/]
  CASCADE_ALLOW_RAW_RPC      Set 0 to disable the API console and /RPC2 [1]
  CASCADE_ALLOW_DATA_DELETE  Set 0 to forbid deleting downloaded data [1]
  CASCADE_DELETE_ROOTS       Extra :-separated roots data may be deleted from [download +
                             completed dirs]
  CASCADE_MAX_UPLOAD_MB      Maximum combined .torrent file size per upload batch, MiB [64]
  CASCADE_POLL_MS            Backend sampling interval for the rate graph, ms [1000]
  CASCADE_STATE_POLL_MS      How often the torrent list is read while a page is open, ms
                             (100-60000; the UI can override it) [500]
  CASCADE_GAMIFY             Set 0 to remove levels, badges and celebrations [1]
  CASCADE_WEB_ROOT           Directory the built UI is served from [/app/web]

ESCAPE HATCHES
  Settings given as environment variables are applied over XML-RPC at startup rather than
  written into rtorrent.rc, so changes made in the UI last until the container restarts.
  RT_EXTRA_CONFIG            Raw rtorrent.rc lines appended to the generated config [unset]
  RT_EXTRA_CONFIG_FILE       File of extra rtorrent.rc lines to append [unset]
  RT_CONFIG_FILE             Use this rtorrent.rc verbatim instead of generating one
                             [/config/rtorrent.rc]
  RT_CONFIG_KEEP             Set 0 to regenerate RT_CONFIG_FILE on every start [1]
  CASCADE_BOOT_SETTINGS      Where the entrypoint stages the settings it hands the server
                             [/run/cascade/boot-settings.json]

Full documentation: https://github.com/JohanLindvall/Cascade
